WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:05.470
Let's say that we wanted to
compute 78 divided by 12.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.170
What would this be?

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.850
Pause this video and
try to figure that out.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.400
Well, one way to think about it is,

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.330
this is the same thing as 78

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.710
divided by 12, heh.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.430
I know when I said it in
English, it sounds the same,

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.810
but here, on the right,
I've written it as 78/12,

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.500
or 78 divided by 12.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.260
Now, how can we re-express this?

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:31.350
Well, let's think about it.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.280
Is there a multiple of 12 that's near 78

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.350
without going above it?

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:38.210
Well, we know that 12 times five is 60,

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.040
12 times six is 72,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.320
12 times seven is 84, so
12 times seven is too high,

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.000
but we can write this
numerator as, instead of 78,

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.370
I can write it as a multiple of 12

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.670
plus whatever's left over.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.410
So, 72 plus six, that's
the same thing as 78,

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.930
so it's that divided by 12,

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.500
and, so, I can write this as,

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.290
I can write the 72/12,

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:07.600
so this is equal to 72 over 12

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.580
plus six over 12,

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.767
plus six over 12 or plus 6/12.

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.520
Now, what's 72 over 12?

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:20.680
We know that 72 is the
same thing as six times 12.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.436
So, this is going to be
six times 12 divided by 12,

00:01:24.436 --> 00:01:27.220
well, that's just going
to simplify to six,

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.880
and then what is six 12ths?

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.860
Well, you might recognize
six as half of 12

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.590
or you could divide the numerator

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.660
and the denominator both by six.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.050
Either way, you are going to get 1/2.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.880
So, you can view this as six plus 1/2

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.540
or you could view this as six and a half,

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.970
and a lot of times, or as
you get more used to this,

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.100
you won't go do all of these steps,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.261
but I want to make sure
you really understand

00:01:51.261 --> 00:01:52.930
what's going on.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:56.200
So, this is the same
thing as six and a half,

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.720
and if I wanted to
express that as a decimal,

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:03.720
that's the same thing as six
ones and then how many tenths?

00:02:04.261 --> 00:02:08.900
Well, 1/2 is the same thing as 5/10,

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.240
so six and 5/10.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.073
So, there you go!

00:02:12.073 --> 00:02:13.890
That's one way of trying to compute

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.300
what 78 divided by 12 is.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.370
Let's do another example.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:22.370
Let's say we wanted to compute
what 20 divided by 80 is.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.810
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.208
Well, we could use a similar technique.

00:02:27.208 --> 00:02:30.510
We could say, hey, this is
the same thing as 20 80ths,

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.430
or we could write 20 the
numerator and 80 the denominator,

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.280
so it's the same thing
as 20 divided by 80,

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:42.840
and then we could think about, well,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.960
how can we simplify this fraction,

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.940
or re-express it in some way?

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:47.773
Well, let's see.

00:02:47.773 --> 00:02:51.460
We can write the numerator as...

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:55.130
We could write this numerator
as equal to one times 20,

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:59.660
and then we could write the
denominator as four times 20,

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.810
as four times 20.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:06.340
And, so, you could just view
this as being equal to 1/4,

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.276
this is equal to 1/4,

00:03:09.276 --> 00:03:12.295
times 20 over 20.

00:03:12.295 --> 00:03:15.650
Times 20 over 20, well, what's 20 over 20?

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:16.973
Well, that's just one.

00:03:16.973 --> 00:03:21.130
That's just one, so this
all just becomes 1/4.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:24.800
Now, how would we express
that as a decimal?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.720
Well, let's see, it's hard to
express 1/4 in terms of tenths

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.180
'cause four doesn't divide easily into 10,

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:34.290
but you can express it
in terms of hundredths.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:38.330
So, 1/4 is the same thing
as 25 over a hundred.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.463
That's the same thing as 25/100.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:44.570
Lemme write it down here
so that I get more space.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:48.820
So, 1/4 is the same thing as 25 over 100,

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.148
and you could get that by
multiplying the numerator

00:03:51.148 --> 00:03:53.037
and the denominator here by 25,

00:03:53.037 --> 00:03:55.000
and the reason why I care about hundredths

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.150
is we know how to represent
hundredths as decimals.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:03.150
This is going to be the same
thing as zero ones and 25/100.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.630
And, so, 20 divided by
80 is 0.25, or 25/100.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:11.131
So, once again, these are
all different strategies

00:04:11.131 --> 00:04:13.890
for thinking about how
we can divide numbers

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.753
that result in decimals.

